ouisiana, Mississippi and Arkansas. This segment provides its products and services through funeral homes and independent agents. It also provides accident and health insurance policies. Citizens, Inc. was founded in 1969 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jon Scott Stenberg | President CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 243 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $72K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Citizens, Inc. is a micro-cap financial services business with a $209M market cap on $256M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $18M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 72% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7170044723570272},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 34% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Citizens reports Q3 results (NYSE:CIA)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667833-citizens-reports-q3-results","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793953742.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Champion Iron (ASX:CIA) Through the Worst as Its High-Grade Ramp-Up Rolls On?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/commodity/iron-ore/is-champion-iron-asxcia-through-the-worst-as-its-high-grade-ramp-up-rolls-on","date":"2026-11-06"